choosing investments the project must meet the highest standards

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:36.080
of environmental protection and bring benefit to the country's

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.480
economic and societal development and people's livelihoods .

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:42.360
We've gone through experiences when governments change. 

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:45.400
They put our projects on hold and review them again as long as

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.480
they're good for the country and they're a win win. 

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:51.640
Everyone will go ahead. Some media have different views but I think it's

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:53.800
because of a lack of understanding. 

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:59.200
The European Union still hasn't officially signed 
off on the Belt Road initiative. 

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:04.200
They point to concerns around the transparency of the bidding process

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:09.040
around environmental issues. Are those concerns justified?

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:12.680
We need to promote mutual understanding and in this

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:16.000
respect we also need to work with companies in Western countries

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:19.560
including those in Europe. If we can strengthen our cooperation

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:23.040
I think transparency will increase. So we're working with

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:24.600
Europe on many projects .

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:30.440
I'm curious how do you respond to allegations of corruption and

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:34.480
fraud that have been levelled at your company and some of its

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:38.720
projects involved and linked to the Belt Road initiative. 

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.280
We don't allow and do not have any corrupt

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:46.040
behaviors related to any official because we know that this kind

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:49.680
of corruption is not going to help with the company's sustainable development. 

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:52.120
And as a listed company we're subject

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:56.400
to market supervision. If there's corrupt behavior the company

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.080
is finished on this. We are very clear .

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:04.720
Because critics of the Belt Road initiative still point to what

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.240
they would say is a lack of transparency around some of the projects. 

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:12.520
What they would say is lack of hiring of local labor

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:16.160
versus Chinese labor. And then ultimately many of these

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:21.120
projects leave the country's heavily indebted to China. 

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:24.440
That would be the criticism. There is some truth in that criticism .

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.840
On the whole I think the situation will

00:21:27.880 --> 00:21:30.320
become more transparent as the Belt Road initiative progresses

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.520
on the issue of pushing up debt .

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.520
Some countries do have relatively higher borrowing .

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:40.440
I don't think that's scary as long as the country's 
economy is growing enough to digest it.

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:43.360
 It's important to see whether the

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.160
debt funded projects are good for the country's economic development 

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:49.360
Of course, I think it's necessary for developed nations

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.960
 to offer financial aid to countries that lack

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:56.360
development capability. As for labor currently my overseas

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:57.720
ratio is at least one to 10 in my company .

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:02.440
There's one Chinese person employed for every 10 foreigners .

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:07.160
The labor cost of a Chinese employee is much higher than that for a local. 

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.200
Many developing countries are still catching up

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:14.040
and their cost of labor is lower than ours. Therefore from the

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:17.160
company's perspective we want to localize as much as possible

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:20.320
hire local people and use fewer Chinese .

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:24.040
I can't say there are no problems. All that we're perfect. 

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:26.800
But the reality is it's not as people say either .

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:29.600
I think it's because of a lack of understanding 

00:22:31.600 --> 00:22:33.800
For both Europe and China .

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:36.520
the potential for business opportunities around the belt and

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:41.360
road initiative are significant. Yet too often a lack of

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:46.120
transparency is stoking concerns fueled by the fact that many of

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:48.400
the big Chinese companies involved are state owned .

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:53.240
China needs to realize that the way that it sees its belt and

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:57.560
road initiative is not necessarily the way other countries see

00:22:57.560 --> 00:22:59.440
their belt and road initiative .

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.280
This is very important for China. It is now present Xi Jinping

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:06.600
flagship international program.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:09.560
 It's embedded in the Chinese constitution .

00:23:09.840 --> 00:23:12.920
The international community I think should look at the Belt Road

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.000
initiative and figure out where countries can partner with China

00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:20.480
where they will maintain and meet the international standards

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:24.920
that we hold so dearly and where they're not. We ought to be

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:28.480
stepping forward to put credible alternative proposals forward

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:33.640
that maintain those high international standards that have

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:37.880
transparency sustainability of projects and have the labor and

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:39.080
environmental standards that we care so deeply about .

00:23:48.920 --> 00:23:52.040
Europe's leaders are trying to remain open minded about the

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:56.320
potential opportunities around China's Belt and Road Initiative

00:23:56.480 --> 00:24:00.240
But it's clear that locking in full EU support will require

00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:04.240
Beijing to translate rhetoric into reality particularly around

00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:08.240
issues of transparency sustainability and inclusiveness. 

00:24:08.680 --> 00:24:12.040
Some European firms are hungrily eyeing dividends but those are

00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:17.960
likely still years away. I'm Tom Mackenzie. Thanks for watching .

